Usage: openbuff run [options] [prompt...]

Run an agent non-interactively on a prompt and exit (headless/CI mode)

Arguments:
  prompt                  Prompt to send; omitted or a lone - reads stdin

Options:
  --approval-mode <mode>  Command approvals: balanced (routine commands run
                          freely), strict, or allow-all (no prompts) (choices:
                          "balanced", "strict", "allow-all")
  --json                  Emit machine-readable events (one JSON object per
                          line) on stdout
  --agent <id>            Run a specific agent id (default: base2)
  --trust-project-agents  Trust this project (agents, skills, MCP config and
                          openbuff.json); recorded as an explicit grant
  --output-schema <file>  Require a bounded JSON object output schema; print
                          validated JSON or a final --json result event
  --model <id>            Primary provider/model for this run and its
                          descendants; does not change configuration
  --timeout <seconds>     Abort the run after this many seconds (default: no
                          timeout)
  -p, --prompt <text>     Prompt text (otherwise use positional text or piped
                          UTF-8 stdin)
  --continue [id]         Continue the last saved headless conversation or an
                          explicit session ID; supply a new prompt with -p or
                          stdin
  -h, --help              display help for command
